', resource_name='com.android.systemui:id/mobile_combo', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 85: UIElement(text=None, content_description='Battery 100 percent.', class_name='android.widget.LinearLayout', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=986, x_max=1006, y_min=1, y_max=128), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.android.systemui', resource_name='com.android.systemui:id/battery', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 86: UIElement(text=None, content_description='No internet', class_name='android.widget.ImageView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=853, x_max=931, y_min=43, y_max=85), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.android.systemui', resource_name='com.android.systemui:id/mobile_type', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\n\\nHere are some useful guidelines you need to follow:\\nGeneral\\n- Usually there will be multiple ways to complete a task, pick the easiest one. Also when something does not work as expected (due to various reasons), sometimes a simple retry can solve the problem, but if it doesn't (you can see that from the history), try to switch to other solutions.\\n- Sometimes you may need to navigate the phone to gather information needed to complete the task, for example if user asks \\\"what is my schedule tomorrow\\\", then you may want to open the calendar app (using the `open_app` action), look up information there, answer user's question (using the `answer` action) and finish (using the `status` action with complete as goal_status).\\n- For requests that are questions (or chat messages), remember to use the `answer` action to reply to user explicitly before finish! Merely displaying the answer on the screen is NOT sufficient (unless the goal is something like \\\"show me ...\\\").\\n- If the desired state is already achieved (e.g., enabling Wi-Fi when it's already on), you can just complete the task.\\nAction Related\\n- Use the `open_app` action whenever you want to open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed), do not use the app drawer to open an app unless all other ways have failed.\\n- Use the `input_text` action whenever you want to type something (including password) instead of clicking characters on the keyboard one by one. Sometimes there is some default text in the text field you want to type in, remember to delete them before typing.\\n- For `click`, `long_press` and `input_text`, the index parameter you pick must be VISIBLE in the screenshot and also in the UI element list given to you (some elements in the list may NOT be visible on the screen so you can not interact with them).\\n- Consider exploring the screen by using the `scroll` action with different directions to reveal additional content.\\n- The direction parameter for the `scroll` action can be confusing sometimes as it's opposite to swipe, for example, to view content at the bottom, the `scroll` direction should be set to \\\"down\\\". It has been observed that you have difficulties in choosing the correct direction, so if one does not work, try the opposite as well.\\nText Related Operations\\n- Normally to select some text on the screen: <i> Enter text selection mode by long pressing the area where the text is, then some of the words near the long press point will be selected (highlighted with two pointers indicating the range) and usually a text selection bar will also appear with options like `copy`, `paste`, `select all`, etc. <ii> Select the exact text you need. Usually the text selected from the previous step is NOT the one you want, you need to adjust the range by dragging the two pointers. If you want to select all text in the text field, simply click the `select all` button in the bar.\\n- At this point, you don't have the ability to drag something around the screen, so in general you can not select arbitrary text.\\n- To delete some text: the most traditional way is to place the cursor at the right place and use the backspace button in the keyboard to delete the characters one by one (can long press the backspace to accelerate if there are many to delete). Another approach is to first select the text you want to delete, then click the backspace button in the keyboard.\\n- To copy some text: first select the exact text you want to copy, which usually also brings up the text selection bar, then click the `copy` button in bar.\\n- To paste text into a text box, first long press the text box, then usually the text selection bar will appear with a `paste` button in it.\\n- When typing into a text field, sometimes an auto-complete dropdown list will appear. This usually indicating this is a enum field and you should try to select the best match by clicking the corresponding one in the list.\\n\\n\\nNow output an action from the above list in the correct JSON format, following the reason why you do that. Your answer should look like:\\nReason: ...\\nAction: {\\\"action_type\\\":...}\\n\\nYour Answer:\\n\",\nevidence/native_run/actions/actions.json:584:            \"content\": \"Reason: Gym Membership is still not visible in the Expense Logs list, and the current view is showing older items around Oct 9\\u20136, so the next step is to continue scrolling down within the scrollable expense list to search for it.\\nAction: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}\",\nevidence/native_run/actions/actions.json:624:    \"summary\": \"Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Scrolled down within the expense list (RecyclerView) to keep searching for \\u201cGym Membership\\u201d because it wasn\\u2019t visible; the view moved from mostly Oct 9\\u20136 entries like Pest Control/Coffee/Dental Care to older Oct 6\\u20134 items like Dental Care, Taxi Fare, Fundraising Events, Consulting Fees, and Gym Membership/Restaurant Meal/Movie Night are still not visible, so continue scrolling down rather than deleting anything yet.\"\nevidence/native_run/actions/actions.json:627:    \"action_output\": \"Reason: Gym Membership is still not visible in the expense list, and the list is currently around Oct 6\\u20134 entries, so the next best step is to continue scrolling down within the RecyclerView to search for it.\\nAction: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}\",\nevidence/native_run/actions/actions.json:628:    \"action_prompt\": \"You are an agent who can operate an Android phone on behalf of a user. Based on user's goal/request, you may\\n- Answer back if the request/goal is a question (or a chat message), like user asks \\\"What is my schedule for today?\\\".\\n- Complete some tasks described in the requests/goals by performing actions (step by step) on the phone.\\n\\nWhen given a user request, you will try to complete it step by step. At each step, a list of descriptions for most UI elements on the current screen will be given to you (each element can be specified by an index), together with a history of what you have done in previous steps. Based on these pieces of information and the goal, you must choose to perform one of the action in the following list (action description followed by the JSON format) by outputing the action in the correct JSON format.\\n- If you think the task has been completed, finish the task by using the status action with complete as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"complete\\\"}`\\n- If you think the task is not feasible (including cases like you don't have enough information or can not perform some necessary actions), finish by using the `status` action with infeasible as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"infeasible\\\"}`\\n- Answer user's question: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"answer\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"<answer_text>\\\"}`\\n- Click/tap on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Long press on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"long_press\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Type text into an editable text field (specified by its index), this action contains clicking the text field, typing in the text and pressing the enter, so no need to click on the target field to start: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": <text_input>, \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`\\n- Press the Enter key: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"keyboard_enter\\\"}`\\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_home\\\"}`\\n- Navigate back: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_back\\\"}`\\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": <up, down, left, right>, \\\"index\\\": <optional_target_index>}`\\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": <name>}`\\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"wait\\\"}`\\n\\nThe current user goal/request is: Delete the following expenses from pro expense: Gym Membership, Restaurant Meal, Movie Night.\\n\\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\\nStep 1: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": \\\"Pro Expense\\\"}. Opened Pro Expense from the home screen as intended; the launcher view changed to the app\\u2019s main screen (package `com.arduia.expense`), so next continue inside the app to find and delete Gym Membership, Restaurant Meal, and Movie Night.\\nStep 2: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 3}. Scrolled down within the main expense list (RecyclerView) to look for Gym Membership/Restaurant Meal/Movie Night since they were not visible; the view shifted lower and now shows a MORE button plus the same recent items repositioned, so the targets are still not on screen and more scrolling is needed.\\nStep 3: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 12}. Tapped the MORE button on Home to open the full Expense Logs list because the target items weren\\u2019t in Recent; this worked, and now older entries including Restaurant Meal and Movie Night are visible with delete icons, so next search/scroll for Gym Membership and delete the three targets from this logs screen.\\nStep 4: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 52}. Clicked the icon beside visible \\u201cRestaurant Meal\\u201d intending to delete it, but it opened the Expense Detail sheet for Restaurant Meal (with its own delete button), so the list item wasn\\u2019t deleted yet and next step should use the detail view\\u2019s delete control.\\nStep 5: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 3}. Tapped the delete icon for \\u201cRestaurant Meal\\u201d in Expense Detail, and it worked: a \\u201cDelete Items\\u201d confirmation dialog with a CONFIRM button appeared; next step should be to tap CONFIRM to finish deleting this expense.\\nStep 6: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Tapped CONFIRM on the delete dialog to finalize the pending deletion; the dialog closed and returned to the Expense Logs list, indicating the delete likely succeeded, but Movie Night is still visible so more target expenses remain to be deleted.\\nStep 7: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 73}. Tapped the visible delete icon for \\u201cMovie Night\\u201d in the Expense Logs list, but instead of deleting it the app opened the Expense Detail sheet for \\u201cMovie Night\\u201d with a separate delete button (btn_delete), so the item is not deleted yet and the next step should use that detail-sheet delete control.\\nStep 8: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 3}. Tapped the delete icon for the \\u201cMovie Night\\u201d expense in Expense Detail, and it worked: a \\u201cDelete Items\\u201d confirmation dialog with a CONFIRM button appeared, so the next step should be to confirm deletion.\\nStep 9: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Tapped CONFIRM on the \\u201cDelete Items\\u201d dialog to finalize the current expense deletion (intended for \\u201cMovie Night\\u201d); the dialog closed and the app returned to the Expense Logs list, so the deletion appears successful and the next step should be to verify/delete any remaining target items (Gym Membership, Restaurant Meal) if still present.\\nStep 10: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Scrolled down the expense list to keep searching for the remaining target \\u201cGym Membership\\u201d; the view jumped to older entries (e.g., ProDev, Home Insurance, Food Delivery, Fine Dining, Bike Repairs), so the scroll worked but Gym Membership is still not visible and more scrolling/search is needed.\\nStep 11: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Scrolled down within the expense list (RecyclerView) to keep searching for \\u201cGym Membership\\u201d since \\u201cRestaurant Meal\\u201d and \\u201cMovie Night\\u201d were not visible; the view jumped from entries around Oct 12\\u20138 (e.g., ProDev/Home Insurance/Fine Dining) to older entries around Oct 9\\u20136 (e.g., Pest Control, Coffee, Miscellaneous Gifts, Therapy Sessions), so the scroll worked but Gym Membership is still not visible and we should continue scrolling down.\\nStep 12: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"down\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Scrolled down within the expense list (RecyclerView) to keep searching for \\u201cGym Membership\\u201d because it wasn\\u2019t visible; the view moved from mostly Oct 9\\u20136 entries like Pest Control/Coffee/Dental Care to older Oct 6\\u20134 items like Dental Care, Taxi Fare, Fundraising Events, Consulting Fees, and Gym Membership/Restaurant Meal/Movie Night are still not visible, so continue scrolling down rather than deleting anything yet.\\n\\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\\nUI element 0: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.ImageButton', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=0, x_max=147, y_min=128, y_max=275), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.arduia.expense', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 1: UIElement(text='Expense Logs', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=189, x_max=526, y_min=138, y_max=209), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.arduia.expense', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 2: UIElement(text='2023 Oct 1 - 15 . DESC